{ Now the smothered mate. His own pieces build the cage around his king. } 20... Kh8 { He is forced into the corner — there is nowhere else to go. Now give up the queen on g eight. [%cal Ye6g8] } 21. Qg8+ { A whole queen for one square. He must take, and the rook fills g eight. [%csl Rg8] } (21. Nf7+ { The check comes first and the mate walks away. } 21... Rxf7 22. Qxf7 Qxa1 23. Nd2 Qe5+ { You won a pawn and lost the game. }) (21. Qe7 { A strong looking square, but he grabs your rook. } 21... Qxa1 22. Nf7+ Rxf7 23. Qxf7 Qxb1 { Everything hangs and there is no mate. }) (21. Qxa6 { A free pawn at a huge price. } 21... Rxa6 22. Ng4 Qxa1 23. Nd2 Rxa2 { A rook down and lost. }) 21... Rxg8 { Forced. Now the knight lands where nothing can touch it. [%cal Yh6f7] } 22. Nf7# { Mate! His own rook and pawns are the walls. That is the smothered mate. [%csl Rh8,Gg8,Gg7,Gh7] } (22. Nxg8 { You take the rook and the mate is gone. } 22... Qxa1 23. f4 Qxb1 24. Nf6 gxf6 { A whole rook behind, and worse coming. }) (22. Nf5 { You rescue the knight from nothing at all. } 22... Qxa1 23. Nd2 Qe5+ 24. Ng3 Qf4 { The mate was on f seven. Now you are lost. }) 1-0


