{ Now the ladder mate. Two rooks walk the king to the wall, one line at a time. [%cal Ye1g1] } 1. Rg1+ { He must step over. Your other rook already owns the next line. [%csl Gf2] } (1. Rf4+ { The rook parks right beside the king with nobody guarding it. } 1... Kxf4 2. Kg2 Kf5 3. Kf3 { One rook still mates, but that was a free gift. }) (1. Rg2+ { A check, but now his king walks straight at your rook. } 1... Kf3 2. Kh2 Kf4 3. Rf2+ { You had to run away. The ladder lost three moves. }) (1. Re4+ { Also a check, and also winning. But you push him along, not to the wall. } 1... Kg5 2. Re1 Kg4 3. Rg1+ { Back to the same idea, one move later. }) 1... Kh3 { One step from the edge. Now the second rook climbs. [%cal Yf2h2] } 2. Rh2# { Mate! Two rooks, one ladder, no way out. [%csl Rh3] } (2. Rg3+ { Careful. His king is standing right next to that square. } 2... Kxg3 3. Rf8 Kg4 4. Kh2 { A whole rook for nothing. You can still mate, very slowly. }) (2. Rf3+ { A check that pushes him back to the fourth row. } 2... Kh4 3. Rg7 Kh5 4. Rh3# { You mate anyway, two moves late. }) 1-0


