{ King and queen against a bare king. The queen cannot do it alone, so use your king. [%cal Yb1b7] } 1. Qb7 { The queen owns the whole seventh rank. His king has two squares left. [%csl Rf8,Rh8] } (1. Qh7+ { Never park the queen where the king can eat her. } 1... Kxh7 { The queen is gone and a lone king cannot mate. Draw. [%csl Rh7] }) (1. Qb8+ { A check, but he just steps away and you start again. } 1... Kh7 2. Qb7+ Kh6 3. Qh1# { You mate anyway, one move later. }) (1. Qb3+ { A check from far away. He runs to the corner. } 1... Kh8 2. Qb7 Kg8 3. Qg7# { Fine, but taking the seventh rank at once was quicker. }) (1. Qg6+ { Also fine. He hides on f eight and you mate at once. } 1... Kf8 2. Qf7# { Same mate, same idea. }) (1. Qa2+ { A check along the long diagonal. He runs for the corner. } 1... Kh8 2. Qa7 Kg8 3. Qg7# { You get there, only slower. }) (1. Qg1+ { A check up the g column. He simply steps aside. } 1... Kf8 2. Qg7+ Ke8 3. Qe7# { Also mate, two moves late. }) 1... Kf8 { He has no squares left. Now step the queen right next to him. [%cal Yb7f7][%csl Gf6] } 2. Qf7# { Mate! The queen kisses him and your king guards her. [%csl Gf6,Rf8] } (2. Qb8# { That is mate as well, from the far end of the rank. Well spotted. }) (2. Qa8# { Mate from the corner. The whole last rank does the job. }) (2. Qc8# { Also mate. Any square on that rank works here. }) (2. Qe7+ { A check, and the mate arrives next move. } 2... Kg8 3. Qg7# { Well played, just one move slower. }) (2. Qg7+ { Almost. He slides across and you mate on the other side. } 2... Ke8 3. Qe7# { Mate in the end. }) (2. Qb4+ { A check from far away. He walks to the corner. } 2... Kg8 3. Qh4 Kf8 4. Qh8# { You mate, but the kiss on f seven was there at once. }) 1-0


