{ His king has marched out to the fourth row, and your queen is close enough to finish him. Mate in two. } 37. Qxb7 { He grabs a pawn on b seven, not worried about his own king. } Qf4+ { The queen sits right beside him, and the pawn on g five guards her. [%csl Gg5] } (37... Qxf6 { You take the pawn and the mate goes with it. } 38. Qe4+ Kg7 39. b4 Qd6 40. b5 { He is fine again. }) (37... Qe6+ { A check, but the wrong one. } 38. Kh5 Qxf6 39. Qe4+ Kg8 40. b4 { The net has gone. }) (37... Kg6 { You bring your king up. That was not the plan here. } 38. Qe4+ Kxf6 39. h4 Qc5 40. Qh7 { Now you are the one being chased. }) 38. Kh5 { His king has nowhere else to go. } Qh4# { Mate! The little pawn on g five does all the guarding. That is the queen kiss again. [%csl Gg5,Rh5] } (38... Qxf6 { The pawn again, with mate in one on the board. } 39. Qe4+ Kg8 40. b4 Kg7 { The win is gone. }) (38... Qf5+ { A check that hands him everything. } 39. Qxf7+ Kh8 40. Qg7# { Now he is the one mating. }) 0-1


