{ Your knight on e four is hanging, but his king is still stuck in the middle. Mate in two. } 10. fxe4 { He grabs the knight, and forgets about his own king. } Qh4+ { Check, and his king has exactly one square. } (10... Qg5 { An attacking square, but he just develops and lives. } 11. Nf3 Qf4 12. O-O h5 13. g5 { He has castled to safety, and now your queen must run instead. }) (10... Nd7 { A quiet developing move with mate in two on the board. } 11. Nf3 h5 12. g5 O-O 13. b4 { You gave the whole win back. }) (10... h5 { You open the h column, but it is far too slow. } 11. Nf3 hxg4 12. hxg4 Rxh1+ 13. Bxh1 { Just a normal game now. }) 11. Kf1 { His king has only one square to run to. } Qf2# { Mate! Your own pawn on e three guards the queen. The queen kiss works even in the opening. [%csl Ge3,Rf1] } (11... O-O { You castle with mate in one available. } 12. Qe1 Qf6+ 13. Nf3 Qf4 { A whole win thrown away. }) (11... Qg3 { So close, but that square is not mate. } 12. Qe1 Qf4+ 13. Nf3 O-O { He wriggles out. }) (11... Qf6+ { A check, and he blocks it easily. } 12. Nf3 Nd7 13. Na4 Bxe4 { The mate has gone. }) 0-1
